{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01RENAj5AbAUDGXTyrRDWPfo","type":"tool_result","content":"package worker\n\nimport \"strings\"\n\n// CommitType maps an issue's type:* label to a conventional-commit type:\n// type:feature is feat, type:bug is fix, and docs, chore, refactor and test\n// keep their names. Any other label, or none, is chore.\nfunc CommitType(labels []string) string {\n\tfor _, l := range labels {\n\t\tswitch strings.ToLower(l) {\n\t\tcase \"type:feature\":\n\t\t\treturn \"feat\"\n\t\tcase \"type:bug\":\n\t\t\treturn \"fix\"\n\t\tcase \"type:docs\":\n\t\t\treturn \"docs\"\n\t\tcase \"type:chore\":\n\t\t\treturn \"chore\"\n\t\tcase \"type:refactor\":\n\t\t\treturn \"refactor\"\n\t\tcase \"type:test\":\n\t\t\treturn \"test\"\n\t\t}\n\t}\n\treturn \"chore\"\n}\n\tExec   bool   // commit as 100755 (only with Src)\n\tDelete bool\n}\n\n// CodeRequest is one worker code commit on a worker/ branch.\ntype CodeRequest struct {\n\tIssue  int        // > 0 (dry-run: < 0 allowed, synthetic result, as Request)\n\tRole   string     // ^[a-z0-9][a-z0-9-]*$\n\tJobID  string     // required: the Ard-Job trailer\n\tType   string     // ^[a-z]{1,16}$, e.g. feat, fix, chore\n\tTitle  string     // untrusted issue title\n\tBody   string     // untrusted summary, already redacted by the caller\n\tBase   string     // 40-hex SHA the job's worktree started from\n\tCreate bool       // the branch must not exist: cut it at Base\n\tFiles  []CodeFile // 1..MaxFiles, unique paths\n}\n\n// ErrBranchExists means a Create found the branch already on the remote.\nvar ErrBranchExists = errors.New(\"committer: branch already exists on the remote\")\n\nconst (\n\tmaxCodeBodyRunes = 4000\n\tzeroSHA          = \"0000000000000000000000000000000000000000\"\n)\n\nvar (\n\ttypeRe = regexp.MustCompile(`^[a-z]{1,16}$`)\n\tshaRe  = regexp.MustCompile(`^[0-9a-f]{40}$`)\n\t// blankRunRe matches three or more consecutive newlines (two blank lines).\n\tblankRunRe = regexp.MustCompile(`\\n{3,}`)\n)\n\n// CodeMessage builds:\n//\n//\t<type>: <title> (#<issue>)\n//\n//\t<body>\n//\n//\tArd-Job: <jobID>\n//\n// Title: control characters, newlines and other whitespace collapse to single\n// spaces; skip-CI tokens and \"skip-checks:\" are defused as in Message; closing\n// references are neutralised; the title part is cut (with \"…\") so the first\n// line is at most 72 runes and always ends in \" (#<issue>)\". An empty title\n// after cleaning is ErrInvalid.\n// Body: \\r\\n and \\r become \\n; other control and format (Cf) characters are\n// dropped; skip-CI tokens defused and references neutralised; runs of more\n// than two blank lines squeezed; cut to 4,000 runes at a line end; trimmed.\n// An empty body leaves out its paragraph. The trailer paragraph is always last.\n// No [skip ci]: PR-branch commits always run CI.\nfunc CodeMessage(typ, title string, issue int, body, jobID string) (string, error) {\n\tswitch {\n\tcase !typeRe.MatchString(typ):\n\t\treturn \"\", fmt.Errorf(\"%w: bad type %q\", ErrInvalid, typ)\n\tcase !jobRe.MatchString(jobID):\n\t\treturn \"\", fmt.Errorf(\"%w: bad or missing job id\", ErrInvalid)\n\tcase issue <= 0:\n\t\treturn \"\", fmt.Errorf(\"%w: issue must be positive\", ErrInvalid)\n\t}\n\tt := strings.Join(strings.FieldsFunc(title, func(r rune) bool {\n\t\treturn unicode.IsSpace(r) || unicode.IsControl(r) || unicode.Is(unicode.Cf, r)\n\t}), \" \")\n\tt = NeutraliseRefs(defuseSkip(t))\n\tif t == \"\" {\n\t\treturn \"\", fmt.Errorf(\"%w: empty title\", ErrInvalid)\n\t}\n\tprefix, suffix := typ+\": \", fmt.Sprintf(\" (#%d)\", issue)\n\tif avail := maxSummaryRunes - utf8.RuneCountInString(prefix+suffix); utf8.RuneCountInString(t) > avail {\n\t\tt = strings.TrimSpace(string([]rune(t)[:avail-1])) + \"…\"\n\t}\n\tmsg := prefix + t + suffix\n\n\tb := strings.ReplaceAll(strings.ReplaceAll(body, \"\\r\\n\", \"\\n\"), \"\\r\", \"\\n\")\n\tb = strings.Map(func(r rune) rune {\n\t\tswitch {\n\t\tcase r == '\\n':\n\t\t\treturn r\n\t\tcase r == '\\t':\n\t\t\treturn ' '\n\t\tcase unicode.IsControl(r) || unicode.Is(unicode.Cf, r):\n\t\t\treturn -1\n(eval):1: no matches found: --include=*.go\n4. **Run the agent** with `.ard/workers/<role>/prompt.txt` and these untrusted inputs: `.ard-input/<issue#>/issue.md` and `comments.md` (written by the loop, outside `.ard/<issue#>/`, never committed), `.ard/<issue#>/plan.md` when triage wrote one and `.ard/<issue#>/issue.md` when a scanner filed the issue (each only as a regular file, never through a symlink), the triage role files and logs, and, in a fix step, `.ard-input/<issue#>/test-output.log` (the untrusted header, the test command and its exit code, and the last 64 KiB of the test log). Review feedback is added by the review-feedback loop. The agent edits code and writes `.ard/<issue#>/worker-<role>.md`; the executor scrubs a stale copy first.\n5. **Guard the diff** after each agent or fix step, before anything leaves the host. The worktree belongs to the agent, so the guard never trusts its `.git`, config, index or attributes: git runs against the controller's own clone with a private index filled from the base commit (so `skip-worktree` and `assume-unchanged` hide nothing, and no planted filter, textconv, fsmonitor or hook runs), with its objects in a private temp directory (the clone is only read, so an agent cannot grow it); a worktree with a new or resized file over 1 MiB, or more than 256 of them, is held before anything is hashed. The scanned bytes are copied to a controller-private directory and the code lane commits the copies, so nothing can change a file between the scan and the commit. Close-out's changed-file listing uses the same hardened path. Paths under `.ard/<issue#>/` and `.ard-input/` belong to close-out and the loop and are left out. Everything else is checked, and any rejection holds the job for a human (`ard:needs-human`, nothing pushed): the path rule in `committer.CheckCodePath` (all of `.github/`, the rest of `.ard/`, `.git` segments, `.gitmodules`, secret-shaped names), any symlink, nested repository or other non-regular file, a file over 1 MiB, a binary file, and more than 256 changed files. The credential scan runs twice: the content of every written file is checked for the values of known secrets (the hold names the variable, never the value), and the built-in pattern scanner runs over it with only the findings on lines this job added kept, so a worker that edits a file that already holds a credential-shaped fixture is not held for lines it did not write. The comment names file, line and rule (`internal/foo_test.go:12: secret scan rule aws-access-key`), never the text. A scanner error fails closed. Test fixtures that look like credentials must be built at run time, as `internal/redact`'s tests do (`\"AK\" + \"IA\" + ...`); a literal is held, and there is no in-band escape. Over 1,000 changed lines in the whole PR (the diff against the merge base with `main`) also holds. The comment shows the reason as `diff guard: <entry>; <entry>; <entry>; and N more`.\n6. **Two commits per round.** The loop commits the code through the committer's code lane (`Branches.CommitCode`) with the title `<type>: <issue title> (#<issue>)`, the redacted summary (secrets and host paths) as the body and an `Ard-Job: <job-id>` trailer, no `[skip ci]`. `<type>` comes from the issue's `type:*` label (`feature` is `feat`, `bug` is `fix`; `docs`, `chore`, `refactor` and `test` keep their names) and is `chore` otherwise. At the end close-out commits `worker-<role>.md` and the redacted logs of every agent step to the same branch (or to `main`, as triage's are, when the job stopped before its first push). `.ard/<issue#>/` never goes through the code lane. A push failure (branch exists, conflict, branch gone, guard) fails the job with no automatic retry.\n7. **Test.** Run `tests` (default `make test`; empty disables the step) as `/bin/sh -c` in the role's image, with no credential. On failure the agent gets the failure output in a fix step, which commits and pushes again, up to `max_test_fixes` (default 2) within the same job. A fix that changes no files, the cap, or the time running out ends the loop with the tests failed. Test logs stay on the host (kept 7 days) and are never committed.\n8. **Open or update a draft PR** with ard's own `Closes #<issue>`, the agent summary quoted and neutralised (`committer.NeutraliseRefs`, then marker and mention defusing), the test result and links to `worker-<role>.md`, the logs and the job id. Reviewers are the role's `reviewers`, or every reviewer role when it is unset or empty (`when:` rules are ignored until #42), plus any `review:<role>` the lead deferred, limited to roles that exist, and requested only when the tests did not fail. The PR stays a draft; the merger marks it ready. A job that has pushed always gets its draft PR, even when it then ends in `ard:needs-human` or a failure, so pushed work is never left without one.","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"3003e936-8801-41f4-995b-b1a9827b380d","uuid":"75481754-1c08-4b01-bcbb-9de509ee0c15","timestamp":"2026-11-23T11:32:32.387Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"package worker\n\nimport \"strings\"\n\n// CommitType maps an issue's type:* label to a conventional-commit type:\n// type:feature is feat, type:bug is fix, and docs, chore, refactor and test\n// keep their names. Any other label, or none, is chore.\nfunc CommitType(labels []string) string {\n\tfor _, l := range labels {\n\t\tswitch strings.ToLower(l) {\n\t\tcase \"type:feature\":\n\t\t\treturn \"feat\"\n\t\tcase \"type:bug\":\n\t\t\treturn \"fix\"\n\t\tcase \"type:docs\":\n\t\t\treturn \"docs\"\n\t\tcase \"type:chore\":\n\t\t\treturn \"chore\"\n\t\tcase \"type:refactor\":\n\t\t\treturn \"refactor\"\n\t\tcase \"type:test\":\n\t\t\treturn \"test\"\n\t\t}\n\t}\n\treturn \"chore\"\n}\n\tExec   bool   // commit as 100755 (only with Src)\n\tDelete bool\n}\n\n// CodeRequest is one worker code 